2result.sql is more robust:

• It trims both sides of the PID join, preventing missed matches when Person.PID also contains stray spaces.  
• The LEFT JOIN inside NOT EXISTS keeps cast rows whose Person record is missing; these rows are then treated as non‑female, so such movies are not incorrectly marked “female‑only”.  
• COALESCE() converts NULL gender (or missing Person) to a non‑female value, satisfying the requirement that unknown gender must disqualify the movie.  
• It first filters Movie.year to four‑digit numbers, avoiding rows with malformed year strings.

Because of these safeguards, 2result.sql follows the specification more precisely than 1result.sql.

```plaintext
2result.sql
```